// #57: with SACK, loss is found by time (RACK, RFC 8985). A hole below one
// SACKed segment waits a quarter of the minimum RTT for reordering, then
// is resent once; recovery ends with the window halved (PRR, RFC 6937).
0      connect 192.0.2.2:80
+0     > S 0:0(0) <mss 1460,sackOK,nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 0,nop,wscale 8,eol>
+0.01  < S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 1
+0     send 14600
+0     > P. 1:1461(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 1461:2921(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 2921:4381(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 4381:5841(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 5841:7301(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 7301:8761(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 8761:10221(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 10221:11681(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 11681:13141(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 13141:14601(1460) ack 1
// Segment 1 is lost; segment 2 arrives. Not lost yet: reordering may still
// bring it within 2.5 ms (min_rtt / 4), so the reordering timer runs.
+0.01  < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <sack 1461:2921>
+0.01  > P. 1:1461(1460) ack 1
+0     < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <sack 1461:7301>
+0     < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <sack 1461:14601>
+0.01  < . 1:1(0) ack 14601 win 65535
// Ten segments in flight before, half after: the window is 5.
+0     send 14600
+0     > P. 14601:16061(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 16061:17521(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 17521:18981(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 18981:20441(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 20441:21901(1460) ack 1
// Congestion avoidance from here: one segment more per window.
+0.01  < . 1:1(0) ack 21901 win 65535
+0     > P. 21901:23361(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 23361:24821(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 24821:26281(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 26281:27741(1460) ack 1
+0     > P. 27741:29201(1460) ack 1
+0.01  < . 1:1(0) ack 29201 win 65535
+0.5   status 1
